# The window's switches for playing the opening from the keyboard and mouse
# (spec/play.md, One command to play): every switch the earlier steps' window
# runs used, with the person's mode. Read with --args, one argument a line.
# The repository keeps no game record ids, so a second, local argument file
# gives what names the game's records: the manifest, the data folder, the
# start cell, --eye and --look, --play-run (the opening's new-game switches)
# and --play-out, the named platforms (--play-elevator,
# --play-elevator-also-with) and the doors the person opens by activating
# them (--play-activate-opens) and the references whose timed activations
# the person's E stands for (--play-activate-person). Give it first:
#   fo4-view --args opening.local.args --args apps/fo4-view/presets/play-opening.args
--under-hypotheses
--walk
--terrain
--around
1
--no-stream
# The person's mode: the keys drive play_run's walker.
--play-keys
--play-stand
0.1
# The walker and its world (play_run's play options).
--walk-speed
300
--play-reach
150
--play-pick-bounds
--play-pick-bounds-activatable
--play-load-doors
--play-follow-grid
--play-slice
0.25
--play-live-world
--play-elevator-door
--play-elevator-held-pose
--play-elevator-rigid
--play-elevator-door-onward
# A ride that ends with the walker in the air ends for it when it lands on
# the ride (play_elevator_end_landing_v1).
--play-elevator-door-landing
# A door the run's scripts close with its activation blocked holds the
# walker until a script opens it (play_door_closed_blocked_holds_v1).
--play-held-doors
# A door the person opens whose reference stores no ONAM is closed from load
# (play_door_closed_at_load_v1): the front door stands before the doorbell.
--play-held-doors-at-load
# A door whose model carries its own frame stands by its collision in its
# open pose: the frame as stored, the parts its sequence named Open moves
# where its last key leaves them (play_door_collision_open_pose_v1): the
# vault doorways' floor is whole and their jambs stop a sideways walk.
--play-door-open-collision
# Such a door is open for the held doors' reading (drawn open, its prompt
# close), and E closes a door that reading shows open and opens again one
# the person closed (play_door_activation_toggles_v1): what is drawn, what
# stops the walker and what the prompt offers are one state.
--play-door-toggle
# A door the reading shows open whose activation the run's scripts last
# blocked is left as it stands by E, no open given to the run, its prompt
# its name alone (play_door_toggle_blocked_unchanged_v1): the house's front
# door during the evacuation.
--play-door-toggle-blocked
# A held door whose reference stores ONAM (open by default) and whose
# collision is not in the walking world is open from load: drawn open, its
# prompt close, E closes it (play_door_stored_open_v1): the house's pocket
# doors and the ruined front doorway.
--play-door-stored-open
# The collision markers' boxes stand where the data places them, taken out
# when the run disables them (play_collision_marker_boxes_v1), but a box
# whose collision layer word is one a walking character passes stays out
# (play_collision_marker_box_layer_passed_v1).
--play-marker-boxes
--play-marker-box-layers
--play-collision-off-chain
--play-collision-reference-alpha
--play-collision-child-flag-agrees
# A static's reference fields XACT, XLRT, XOWN and ONAM do not keep its
# collision out: the checkpoint gate's frame stands beside the gate's box
# (refr_static_fields_collision_unchanged_v1).
--play-collision-static-fields
# E meets what the crosshair enters first (play_activate_ray_first_met_v1).
--play-pick-first-met
# The caller's actions held until a stage keep their offset from it, and the
# person's E stands for the timed activation it replaces
# (caller_action_after_keeps_offset_v1, play_activate_written_second_v1).
--play-action-after-offset
--play-player-moveto
--play-player-sits
# The run's actors as their characters.
--timeline-cast
--timeline-target-rotation
--timeline-child-flag-agrees
--timeline-nowait
--actor-missing-bone-bind
# A bone the skeleton lacks follows the nearest bone of its skin the skeleton
# holds (actor_missing_bone_follows_nearest_v1): hair and skirts stay on the
# head and the body instead of reaching to the feet.
--actor-missing-bone-nearest
--actor-start-clip
--actor-subgraph-keywords
--actor-clip-folder
--actor-subgraph-flag-one
--actor-model-graph-idle
# An actor's part model's effect-shader float controller (a glow) is drawn
# as stored instead of refusing the actor (actor_effect_controller_stored_v1):
# the creatures at the neighbourhood objective stand drawn, not as markers.
--actor-effect-stored
# A placement the draw refuses for its skinned shapes is drawn as one more
# actor by those shapes on its model's own nodes, its editor marker
# subtrees set aside (model_skinned_own_nodes_every_placement_v1): the
# crib's occupant and the seated remains.
--skinned-models-own-nodes
# Of those, a placement whose reference stores a ragdoll pose (XRGD, not
# read) is left out: its model's stored pose is not the pose shown
# (refr_ragdoll_pose_unread_left_out_v1): the checkpoint's skeletons and
# the remains at the vault's exit.
--skinned-models-ragdoll-left-out
# Light, sky and exposure.
--light-cell
--light-inherits
--light-points
--light-reference-radius
--light-fade
--light-fog
--sky-weather
--light-weather
--fog-weather
--assume-hour
11
--assume-weather
0
--exposure-eye
--exposure-eye-floor
# Measured on what the eye sees (the first view is a near wall).
--exposure-eye-visible
# What the drawing reads.
--draw-child-flag-agrees
--draw-platforms
# The doors the held doors' reading holds, shut while held and posed open
# after (play_door_drawn_as_held_v1).
--draw-held-doors
# A static whose reference's XACT, XLRT, XOWN or ONAM alone kept it out is
# drawn (refr_static_fields_render_unchanged_v1), and a static whose model
# turns a leaf off its collision is drawn with the leaf in the pose the
# collision marker boxes meeting it give (play_static_leaf_two_pose_v1): the
# checkpoint gate's frame.
--draw-static-fields
--draw-static-leaves
# A reference whose unread XALP alone kept it out is drawn
# (refr_xalp_render_unchanged_v1): the vault hall ends whose floor and jambs
# --play-collision-reference-alpha already stands in the walking world.
--draw-reference-alpha
# A reference whose scripts kept it out is drawn as its model stores it, the
# run deciding its presence (refr_script_render_as_stored_v1): the nursery's
# lamp, toys, linens and changing table.
--draw-scripted-as-stored
# An activator whose unread marker colour, flags or activate text kept it
# out is drawn as its model stores it (acti_fields_render_unchanged_v1).
--draw-activator-fields
# A furniture whose unread PNAM, FNAM, MNAM, SNAM or WBDT kept it out is
# drawn as its model stores it (furn_fields_render_unchanged_v1): the
# house's beds, chairs and sofa.
--draw-furniture-fields
# The worldspace's persistent references standing in a loaded grid square
# join it (world_persistent_refs_drawn_in_square_v1): the nursery's crib.
--draw-world-persistent
# An activator refused for its animation is drawn by the shapes its
# controllers do not reach, its reference's XLRT set aside
# (acti_unmoved_parts_drawn_v1): the nursery's crib.
--draw-activator-parts
# A static refused only for model blocks no rule settles (a behaviour
# graph, particle systems, blocks the reader does not decode) is drawn by
# the shapes those blocks and its controllers do not reach, the rest left
# out and counted (static_unmoved_parts_drawn_v1): the room the first vault
# lift comes down into, its landing, drop, lower floor and stairs.
--draw-static-parts
# A named platform's skinned shape whose bones go with several parts is
# skinned again as they move (play_platform_skin_follows_parts_v1): the
# elevators' decks and the walkways.
--draw-platform-skins
# A named platform's shape on a node a sequence sets with no part of its own
# goes with the part of the nearest such node above it
# (play_platform_shape_nearest_part_v1): the gear door's hub pieces leave the
# doorway with the gear.
--draw-platform-nearest-part
# The run's actors stand on the named platform's part under them and ride it
# (play_cast_stands_on_platform_v1): the deck's crowd on the deck.
--draw-cast-on-platforms
# Each rides the part it stands on while that part is under it, a cover
# closing over the shaft above it not taken instead
# (play_cast_keeps_its_part_v1): the crowd rides the deck down.
--draw-cast-keeps-its-part
# An actor of the run whose drawn body at the eye's height comes within
# reach of the eye is drawn moved clear of it, eased round the eye
# (play_cast_kept_clear_of_walker_v1): the eye does not enter the
# checkpoint crowd's heads. The run is unchanged.
--draw-cast-keeps-clear
# The worn armours' slots decide what of a head is hidden
# (npc_head_hidden_by_head_slot_v1): the checkpoint's helmets keep faces.
--actor-head-slots
# An actor listing its own head parts takes its race's parts of the types
# its list lacks (npc_head_parts_race_fill_kinds_v1): the checkpoint's
# capped boy has a face, not a mouth alone.
--actor-head-race-fill
# A head part with conditions is drawn when its list holds against the
# stages the run has set, left out alone when it does not
# (npc_head_part_conditions_run_stages_v1): the lab coats' heads.
--actor-head-conditions
# An actor's models read as a placed reference's: a texture missing only in
# slots the frame never samples does not keep the actor out
# (actor_texture_missing_unread_slot_v1): the vault's security staff, whose
# helmet visor's mask texture is in no archive, are drawn.
--actor-unread-texture-slots
# The cast's appearance (owner's order; our assumptions, not read from the
# running game): a templated character takes its traits, outfit and
# keywords through the template slots of bits 0, 8 and 12
# (npc_template_bits_traits_inventory_v1), and each leveled list its chain
# reaches yields the entry seed 1 picks (npc_leveled_entry_seeded_pick_v1):
# looks the seed chose, not the game's.
--actor-template-bits
--actor-leveled-seed
1
